 "note": "The press-two-tabs latch, v5, on the Scout's cartridge and receiver: one push latches it, one squeeze unlatches it. The receiver and cartridge are cut at the tab line and cut away; the sliders, steel pins, spring, guide poles, XT60 and blades are whole. New over v4: a 3 x 16 steel pin in each bolt's bearing corner, 3.0 overlap on a flat ledge with a 20 deg seat ramp (a pull drives the pins outward, so it locks harder the harder you pull), two 3 x 20 steel guide poles beside the XT60 (they engage 11.7 below the seat, the XT60 at 6.0), rest-stop lugs on the tabs, 3.8 travel. Built by parts/latch5/make.py on the vendored latch v4 CAD.",
 "cg_ref": null,
